            <ArticleTitle>[Epidural anesthesia and analgesia in the perioperative treatment of a patient with Kartagener syndrome].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>431-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Kartagener's syndrome is an inherited disease characterized by a triad of symptoms--bronchiectasis, situs inversus and sinusitis--and is classified as an immotile cilia syndrome. Patients may experience specific airway problems when undergoing anesthesia for surgical procedures. We report the case of a woman with Kartagener's syndrome who underwent surgery under epidural anesthesia with postoperative epidural analgesia, both techniques proving successful.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
